OL,4,CGirls fear real life consequences of   
OL,5,Cmisogyny                               
OL,6,GGirls as young as 13 have said         
OL,7,Gmisogynistic behaviour has become so   
OL,8,G"normalised" they are no longer        
OL,9,Gsurprised by it and fear it will never 
OL,10,Gchange.                                
OL,12,FSharing their experiences at a         
OL,13,Fconference in Sunderland organised by  
OL,14,Fa domestic abuse charity, they said    
OL,15,Fboys would call them sexualised names  
OL,16,Fand comment on their bodies but they   
OL,17,Ffelt uncomfortable in challenging this.
OL,19,FSome boys at the event said they might 
OL,20,F"make jokes" but had not realised the  
OL,21,Fimpact this had.                       
OL,22,                                   G2/4 
